  "prefLabel": "Site 102.21 Exemplary natural community",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Site 102.21 “Exemplary natural community” means “exemplary natural community” as defined in RSA 217-A:3, VII, namely, “a viable occurrence of a rare natural community type or a high quality example of a more common natural community type as designated by the natural heritage bureau based on community size, ecological condition, and landscape context.”\n\nSource. #9182, eff 6-17-08; ss by #10993, eff 12-16-15",
